Real-vehicle sessions are coming (owner: Ford baseline today, planted faults Saturday). Make them judge demos with one
command, no hand editing:
1. scripts/export_session_bundle.py <session_id> [--label "Ford F-150 2.7L, MAF unplugged"] [--out NAME.mmrec]: export a
   finished backend session (live or upload mode) to a judge .mmrec: the hash-chained events.jsonl, the adapter
   transcript the phone uploaded, every referenced blob (photos, clips, audio, PDFs), the report with its Wonder review,
   and the cached model responses the session used, so replay is $0 and byte-identical. Full VIN never leaves vin.py
   (truncated only). Refuse if any referenced blob or cached response is missing, naming it. Label "real vehicle, real
   AI outputs" in meta.json.
2. The judge landing lists every bundle in the fixtures dir: real-vehicle bundles first with their label, simulated ones
   after, clearly marked. The primary "Play the investigation" button prefers a real bundle when one exists.
   modal_app seeding already copies new/changed bundles.
3. scripts/import_phone_recording.sh: adb pull of the phone's .mmrec recordings (Recorder.kt output path) into a staging
   dir, verify each (mmrec verify + replay_check), and print the matching export command.
4. Tests: export of a session built by the existing demo generator round-trips (export -> replay -> identical state and
   report), missing-blob refusal, VIN truncation, landing ordering.
5. docs/JUDGES.md is stale: it says "the highest-confidence mask is the match" and "photo bytes are not bundled". Fix
   both to match the current site (no match claimed; photo shown with candidate overlays).
Never print secret values. Keep the backend suite under 3 minutes. Run backend suite, ci_parity.sh, make_demo_bundle.py
--check, replay_check, web build, acceptance_sweep.sh. Add a short "Turning a real session into a judge demo" section to
docs/JUDGES.md (owner-facing) and a DECISIONS entry. Do not commit. Foreground only.
